---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · TEACHING METHODOLOGY — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ THIS IS A COMBINED PAGE, AND THE COMBINATION IS THE CLIENT'S IA.
 * It carries TWO of the brief's fourteen bullets: Teaching Methodology and
 * Collaborative Learning. They belong together because Collaborative learning is
 * not a separate programme at this school — it is the third of the three things
 * the school names as its method. Splitting them produced two thin pages that
 * each had to explain the other.
 *
 * A standalone /collaborative-learning/ route existed briefly as an
 * implementation experiment. Its verified content is merged here and the route
 * is retired.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE — the school's own words ═══════════════════════════════════════
 *   The method, quoted verbatim: "Incorporate Technology, a theory of Multiple
 *     Intelligence and Collaborative learning in all areas of teaching."
 *   The Principal: "All the students do not have the same talents."
 *   The Principal: classrooms are "places of curiosity and collaboration."
 *   100 Microsoft Innovative Educator Experts → a Microsoft Showcase School.
 *
 * ⚠ THE FOUR-MOVE LESSON ("Ask, Do, Discuss, Show") THAT ONCE SAT HERE WAS NOT
 * SUNBEAM'S. It was verified absent from the school's site and removed from
 * three pages and a component. Do not reintroduce it. The school names three
 * things, not four moves, and they are not a lesson shape.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — the panels, the room count and AI as a subject belong to
 * Smart Classrooms & Digital Literacy. Technology appears here ONLY as the first
 * of the three, anchored on the certification, and points there rather than
 * restating it.
 *
 * Composition: statement (paper) → collage (ivory, LEFT — the three) → split
 * (sand, RIGHT — collaboration in practice) → path (paper — multiple
 * intelligence, evidenced) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcStatement from '../../../components/academics/system/AcStatement.astro';
import AcCollage from '../../../components/academics/system/AcCollage.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcPath from '../../../components/academics/system/AcPath.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/activity learning lab/DSC_1215 copy.jpg';
import pEmbroidery from '../../../assets/School Activity in Uniform/Embriodery.jpg';
import pChef from '../../../assets/School Activity in Uniform/School Activity in Uniform (1).jpg';
import pOwn from '../../../assets/School Activity in Uniform/School Activity in Uniform (5).jpeg';
import pActivity from '../../../assets/activity learning lab/DSC_1215 copy.jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Teaching Methodology — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="The method Sunbeam School Ballia names as its own: technology, a theory of multiple intelligence and collaborative learning, built into all areas of teaching rather than run as separate programmes."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Teaching Methodology"
    standfirst="Three things, named by the school — and not one of them is a special lesson."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Teaching & Learning', href: '/academics/teaching-learning/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="The activity learning laboratory at Sunbeam School Ballia, its worktables set out for group work."
    position="50% 50%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcStatement
      ground="paper"
      ghost="3"
      ghostAt="right"
      kicker="The method, in the school’s words"
      statement="In all areas<br /><em>of teaching.</em>"
      body={[
        'Sunbeam Ballia states its method in one sentence, and the last five words are the part that matters: <em>“Incorporate Technology, a theory of Multiple Intelligence and Collaborative learning <strong>in all areas of teaching</strong>.”</em>',
        'Three things, and none of them a timetabled slot. There is no collaboration lesson and no multiple-intelligence week — the claim is that all three run through ordinary teaching, which is a harder thing to promise and a harder thing to fake.',
      ]}
    />

    <AcCollage
      ground="ivory"
      side="left"
      kicker="The three, unpacked"
      heading="Named, and each one<br /><em>anchored to something</em>"
      body={[
        'A method is only worth reading if each part of it points at something checkable. All three of Sunbeam’s do — two to the Principal’s own published words, and one to a certification held by a hundred members of staff.',
      ]}
      ledger={[
        { k: 'Technology', v: '<strong>100 Microsoft Innovative Educator Experts</strong> — the certification that makes Sunbeam a Microsoft Showcase School. The rooms it runs in are set out on Smart Classrooms &amp; Digital Literacy.' },
        { k: 'Multiple Intelligence', v: '“All the students do not have the same talents.” — the Principal.' },
        { k: 'Collaborative learning', v: 'Classrooms as “places of curiosity and collaboration.” — the Principal.' },
      ]}
      lead={{ src: pActivity, alt: `The activity learning laboratory at ${school}, its worktables set out for group work` }}
      support={[
        { src: pEmbroidery, alt: `Students of ${school} working together on embroidery from one shared basket of thread` },
        { src: pOwn, alt: `Two students of ${school} sharing a desk, each working on her own drawing` },
      ]}
    />

    <AcSplit
      ground="sand"
      side="right"
      ratio="wide"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="What collaboration looks like when it is real"
      heading="One basket<br /><em>of thread</em>"
      body={[
        'The word “collaborative” survives on most school sites without ever touching a photograph. Here it does. In the school’s own embroidery session the students are not each issued a kit — they work from <strong>one shared basket of thread</strong>, which means the thing a child needs next is in somebody else’s hand.',
        'The cooking activity is built the same way: one demonstration table, a class in paper chef hats around it, and no version of the task that can be completed alone.',
        'Neither is a lesson called Collaboration. That is the school’s point — it is in the shape of an ordinary activity rather than in a slot on the timetable.',
      ]}
      photo={pEmbroidery}
      alt={`Students of ${school} working together on embroidery from one shared basket of thread`}
      inset={pChef}
      insetAlt={`A teacher at ${school} demonstrating at the table, her class in paper chef hats around her`}
    />

    <AcPath
      ground="paper"
      kicker="And the second of the three"
      heading="Different talents,<br /><em>different platforms</em>"
      body={[
        '“All the students do not have the same talents” is easy to say and expensive to act on — acting on it means running enough different things that a child who is not academic still has somewhere to be good. The school’s own published record is the evidence, and it is unusually wide for a district school.',
      ]}
      beats={[
        { k: 'Speaking', body: 'Class I entered an inter-branch Attire Speak competition; Class IV took the top three places in a group-wide declamation.' },
        { k: 'Making', body: 'Folk painting under Impetus, embroidery, and the Srijan making-and-design room.' },
        { k: 'Building', body: 'The Robotics Lab, and a second place at an international robotics championship.' },
        { k: 'The field', body: 'Kho-kho gold, chess, handball, taekwondo — a sporting record stronger than most.' },
      ]}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Three things,<br /><em>everywhere.</em>"
      body="The school publishes its method, the Principal's words behind two of the three, and the certification behind the first. It does not publish lesson plans, a scheme of work, or an observation framework — so no lesson shape is described here."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Students and staff of ${school} gathered on the hall stage`}
      position="50% 42%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
